{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' papers/README.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Downloaded Papers\n\nPDFs were downloaded to this directory and chunked into `papers/pages/` with the provided PDF chunker at 3 pages per chunk. All PDFs were validated with `pypdf`.\n\n1. [Bongard-LOGO: A New Benchmark for Human-Level Concept Learning and Reasoning](2010.00763_bongard_logo_benchmark.pdf)\n   - Authors: Weili Nie, Zhiding Yu, Lei Mao, Ankit B. Patel, Yuke Zhu, Animashree Anandkumar\n   - Year: 2020/2021\n   - Source: arXiv 2010.00763, NeurIPS 2020\n   - URL: https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.00763\n   - Why relevant: Core synthetic 2D geometry benchmark with repeated positive/negative examples and ground-truth LOGO action programs.\n\n2. [Visual Spatial Reasoning](2205.00363_visual_spatial_reasoning.pdf)\n   - Authors: Fangyu Liu, Guy Emerson, Nigel Collier\n   - Year: 2022/2023\n   - Source: arXiv 2205.00363, TACL 2023\n   - URL: https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.00363\n   - Why relevant: Controlled image-text spatial-relation dataset useful for addressing and relation-verbalization baselines.\n\n3. [PuzzleVQA: Diagnosing Multimodal Reasoning Challenges of Language Models with Abstract Visual Patterns](2403.13315_puzzlevqa_abstract_patterns.pdf)\n   - Authors: Yew Ken Chia, Vernon Toh Yan Han, Deepanway Ghosal, Lidong Bing, Soujanya Poria\n   - Year: 2024\n   - Source: arXiv 2403.13315, Findings ACL 2024\n   - URL: https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.13315\n   - Why relevant: Abstract pattern VQA with ground-truth perception, induction, and deduction explanations.\n\n4. [Reasoning Limitations of Multimodal Large Language Models: A Case Study of Bongard Problems](2411.01173_bongard_reasoning_limitations_mllms.pdf)\n   - Authors: Mikolaj Malkinski, Szymon Pawlonka, Jacek Mandziuk\n   - Year: 2024/2025\n   - Source: arXiv 2411.01173, ICML 2025\n   - URL: https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.01173\n   - Why relevant: Directly evaluates MLLMs on Bongard problems with direct, descriptive, iterative, and contrastive prompting strategies.\n\n5. [Forgotten Polygons: Multimodal Large Language Models are Shape-Blind](2502.15969_forgotten_polygons_shape_blind.pdf)\n   - Authors: William Rudman, Michal Golovanevsky, Amir Bar, Vedant Palit, Yann LeCun, Carsten Eickhoff, Ritambhara Singh\n   - Year: 2025\n   - Source: arXiv 2502.15969, Findings ACL 2025\n   - URL: https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.15969\n   - Why relevant: Controlled evidence that MLLMs fail at simple polygon identification and side-counting, especially for novel shapes.\n\n6. [VisuLogic: A Benchmark for Evaluating Visual Reasoning in Multi-modal Large Language Models](2504.15279_visulogic_visual_reasoning.pdf)\n   - Authors: Weiye Xu et al.\n   - Year: 2025\n   - Source: arXiv 2504.15279\n   - URL: https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15279\n   - Why relevant: Visual-centric reasoning benchmark designed to reduce text-only shortcuts, including spatial and attribute reasoning.\n\n7. [Spatial-DISE: A Unified Benchmark for Evaluating Spatial Reasoning in Vision-Language Models](2510.13394_spatial_dise_benchmark.pdf)\n   - Authors: Xinmiao Huang et al.\n   - Year: 2025/2026\n   - Source: arXiv 2510.13394, ICLR 2026\n   - URL: https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.13394\n   - Why relevant: Taxonomy and dataset for intrinsic/extrinsic, static/dynamic spatial reasoning; useful for evaluation taxonomy.\n\n8. [Symbolic Grounding Reveals Representational Bottlenecks in Abstract Visual Reasoning](2604.21346_symbolic_grounding_bottlenecks.pdf)\n   - Authors: Mohit Vaishnav, Tanel Tammet\n   - Year: 2026\n   - Source: arXiv 2604.21346\n   - URL: https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.21346\n   - Why relevant: Most directly aligned with the hypothesis; compares raw-image VLM performance with LLM reasoning over symbolic LOGO-style descriptions.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
